        "slug": "synapse-data-center-power-plant-project",
        "text": "Proceeding 30732 Register\nApplication 30732-A001\nDecision 30732-D01-2026\nAUC contact: Victor Choy\n403-592-4439 or victor.choy@auc.ab.ca\nSynapse Real Estate Corp: Jason Van Gaal\n613-797-3311 or jason@synapsedatacenter.com\nOverview\nSynapse Real Estate Corp applied to construct and operate a combined-cycle natural gas-fired power plant with a nominal capacity of approximately 1,400 megawatts (MW) as well as 1,800 MW of emergency and backup diesel generation (the power plant). The application stated that the power plant will not be connected to the Alberta Interconnection Electric System but will be used to power the on-site data centre load. The application was filed under the Hydro and Electric Energy Act.\nOn August 17, 2026, the AUC denied the Synapse Data Center Power Plant Project application. The Commission finds that the project is too close to the surrounding community, and Synapse failed to demonstrate any compelling justification for selecting that location. The site is simply not suitable for the proposed development. In making this finding, the Commission is not commenting on the suitability of a data centre in this location. The Commission does not approve or regulate data centres.\nHearing information\nTo learn more about the review process, or for more information about how you may become involved in this proceeding, please contact us or visit the following webpages:\nReview process for facility applications\nHave your say about a utility project\nParticipate in an AUC hearing\nThe eFiling System​\nThe eFiling System should be accessed to view the applications and the other documents the AUC will be considering in this proceeding. The system is also used to file submissions and evidence to participate in the proceeding.\nTo create an account, select “New account” and follow the steps to create a user ID and password. If you have any questions about how to use the eFiling System please contact us at info@auc.ab.ca or 310-4AUC.\nDocuments being considered in this proceeding can be found in the eFiling​ System (which requires log in). Once you have logged in, enter 30732 in the “go to” section at the top left corner of your screen.",
