        "chars": 2242,
        "content": "Notion’s ethos has always been technology meets the liberal arts. To build the best tools for thought, we refuse to treat engineering and design as separate jobs. This shapes what we build and who we hire.\n\nAnd almost no one represents that ethos better than Max Schoening.\n\nWhen Max joined Notion last year, he [described](https://www.notion.com/blog/software-should-bend-welcome-max-schoening) himself as a *Tüftler*, someone who tinkers until something works. This year, he and the team shipped two of our biggest launches: Custom Agents for everyday knowledge workers and our Developer Platform, which lets people and agents extend Notion to fit how they work.\n\nAnd now, Max is stepping into the role of CTO. While Max has been our product and design leader for the last year, he’s an engineer by trade and has built as much as he has designed. He ran design early on at Heroku (the original PaaS) and worked on Cloud Run at Google. At GitHub, he spent six and a half years working on GitHub Issues, Pull Requests, GitHub Actions, and cloud development environments—tools that millions of developers use to build and ship software.\n\nMax has spent his career making complex infrastructure feel simple, mostly for developers. At Notion, he’s doing the same for founders, builders, and businesses of all kinds.\n\nHe believes in open platforms that put customers first. So do we. Openness and agent-neutral context benefit all of our customers, from a small coffee business wrestling with its wholesal",
        "description": "The org chart of the future will be multidisciplinary, and we’re lucky to have Max lead our technical organization into this future.",
