      "response": {
        "desktop_packages": "Download the package for your platform from the\n[Hermes website](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/).\n\n- **Windows:** open the `.appinstaller` download with Windows App Installer.\n  It installs the signed MSIX bundle and records its update source.\n  Microsoft Store packages have separate Store ownership.\n- **macOS:** open the DMG, then copy `Hermes.app` to Applications. The ZIP\n  artifact carries the signed app used by the automatic updater.\n\nBundled packages contain the agent, Python, supported dependencies, and prebuilt\ninterfaces. First launch does not build that base runtime. Provider access and\noptional integrations can still require network access.\n\nA `Hermes-Setup` bootstrap installer is different: it downloads a source\ninstallation and builds the desktop app. See [Hermes Desktop](../user-guide/desktop.md).\n\nThere is no separate remote-only Desktop download. To use Desktop with a Hermes\nbackend on another machine, install one of the packages above and connect it\nfrom **Settings → Gateways**; see\n[Connecting to a remote backend](../user-guide/desktop.md#connecting-to-a-remote-backend).\n\n:::note\nThe macOS installer is **Apple Silicon only**. macOS on x86 (Intel) processors is [not a supported platform](./platform-support.md#unsupported).\n:::",
        "features": [
          {
            "description": "Full TUI with multiline editing, slash-command autocomplete, conversation history, interrupt-and-redirect, and streaming tool output.",
            "title": "A real terminal interface"
          },
          {
            "description": "Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, Signal, and CLI — all from a single gateway process. Voice memo transcription, cross-platform conversation continuity.",
            "title": "Lives where you do"
          },
          {
            "description": "Agent-curated memory with periodic nudges. Autonomous skill creation after complex tasks. Skills self-improve during use. FTS5 session search with LLM summarization for cross-session recall. Honcho dialectic user modeling. Compatible with the agentskills.io open standard.",
            "title": "A closed learning loop"
          },
          {
            "description": "Built-in cron scheduler with delivery to any platform. Daily reports, nightly backups, weekly audits — all in natural language, running unattended.",
            "title": "Scheduled automations"
          },
          {
            "description": "Spawn isolated subagents for parallel workstreams. In Desktop, choose their provider, model, and limits under Settings → Model → Subagents, then Apply the complete route. Write Python scripts that call tools via RPC, collapsing multi-step pipelines into zero-context-cost turns.",
            "title": "Delegates and parallelizes"
          },
          {
            "description": "Six built-in terminal backends — local, Docker, SSH, Modal, Daytona, and Vercel Sandbox — plus plugin backends such as Singularity/Apptainer. Daytona and Modal offer serverless persistence — your agent'"'"'s environment hibernates when idle and wakes on demand, costing nearly nothing between sessions. Run it on a $5 VPS or a GPU cluster.",
            "title": "Runs anywhere, not just your laptop"
          },
          {
            "description": "Batch trajectory generation, trajectory compression for training the next generation of tool-calling models.",
            "title": "Research-ready"
          }
        ],
        "install_commands": [
